{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/327830-rumors-hunters-other-hunters-and-everything-trying-to-kill-them","id":327830,"title":"Rumors: Hunters, other hunters, and everything trying to kill them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-01T22:50:12-08:00","id":327830,"title":"Rumors: Hunters, other hunters, and everything trying to kill them","content":"<a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/download/2ls4xd2jn5bf5pj/World+of+Darkness+Rumors.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mediafire.com/download/2l...ess+Rumors.pdf</a><br /> <br /> Based on this file, I'm spearheading a 2.0 Rumors project to create even more awesome plot hooks, story ideas, and paradigm shifts that anyone can use at their table. If you have an awesome idea for a rumor, story, or legend, post it here, and by next February we'll decide who's story passed the bar to be included.<br /> <br /> This thread is focused on hunters, <i>everything</i> trying to kill them, and the strange things that others want no part of; ideas not pertaining to these in some form will automatically not be included.<br /> <br /> Ready...set...go!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T12:17:49-08:00","id":328533,"title":"","content":"&quot;It always the heart. I don't know why. Maybe it is the symbol of life. Maybe the symbol of love. Maybe it just the colour, or the shape. But the target is always the heart. The weird thing is that the victims are always found smiling, like they had the best moment in their life just before they died. Maybe the heart needs to be filled with joy? I don't know, and I don't care. We need to find that thing and burn it. No, not &quot;him&quot;. It lost the right to be called &quot;human&quot; after it first murder&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Is it me, or that the old coffee shop has changed its logo? New owners, maybe. But I must say, I'm sure I've seen it before...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T23:48:39-08:00","id":328954,"title":"","content":"&quot;To: MRU 9-26 Actual<br /> From: Scarecrow<br /> Re: Facility 28<br /> Facility gone from Heimdallr's sight. Thor advises immediate retrieval. Rendezvous with MRU 5-71 and Einherjar unit at Delta, Charlie Oscar, and proceed to facility. Ensure operational security met. S\u00e6hr\u00edmnir must remain contained. If mission is considered failed, Ragnarok Protocol: Jotunn will engage.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> &quot;We aren't a union, otherwise we would've actually fucking done something by now. Fuck you, I'm serious. Think about it, how many of us are out there that could back each other up? Fuck up the monsters by all going out at once? No, we're too busy hiding, skulking around and beating street dealers and leeches down until the next night, even acting like the morality police. What union honestly just sits around and takes it up the ass from everyone else? I did some digging, I can't find any trace of a Holly Ramirez that died in '97, not one. Tried to trace the web host for the forum, and it's all PO boxes and deserted buildings. And who decides which of us becomes a 'rep' going from city to city? Why should it even matter where we go? Seriously, someone's fucking playing up, and I'm gonna find them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T05:10:49-08:00","id":329117,"title":"","content":"Wake up sheeple:<br /> <br /> &quot;The AkD aren't really hunters, they only say that to throw off real hunters who come across them. They only go after monsters who have stuff they want, otherwise they're just wannabe witches.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Ascending Ones aren't really hunters, they're a cult taking out the competition.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ashwood Abbey aren't really hunters. They've got ghosts in 'em, drunk on living again, that's why they do all the crazy shit they do. You can't trust them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Barret Commission aren't really hunters, they're just in it for themselves. Sure, they'll help as long as they get something out of it, but don't think for a second they won't turn on you and let a monster go if they see profit in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Bear Lodge aren't really hunters. They're werewolves themselves - think about it - live in the sticks, fancy themselves the best trackers ever, take other hunters out into the middle of nowhere where no one'll see 'em again, do I have to draw a picture for you?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you ever met the Cainite Heresy? Seriously, they are <i>not</i> hunters, they're slashers. They go after vamps like the best of them, I grant, but they're nuts. It's only a matter of time before they snap and gut some poor goth kid. Shut up, that was one time.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Cheiron Group's goons aren't hunters like us. They's some new sort of supernatural that's building itself out of bits of the others. I don't even know if they're really part of the Group. Don't trust 'em, anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Division Six aren't really hunters, they're cultists of those things we saw that time in Detroit, the ones talking about principles. That's why they talk that shit about breaks in reality.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The 'Illuminated Brotherhood?' Don't make me laugh. They're not hunters, they using those drug trips to let some spirit or god or something into this world. They should be target no 1.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Keepers of the Source aren't really hunters, and they're not harmless, don't be fooled. All that looking for sacred places? They're looking for fae-touched places, to let their kin across.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Knights of St George aren't really hunters. They right at the centre of things in British power, and you know what means. Reptoids, man; the name's just to throw you off.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Long Night aren't really hunters, they're some crazy apocalypse cult trying to end the world.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Those Loyalists aren't really hunters. It's right there in the name - 'Thule.' And all those dusty books they go after? Mark my words, there's something ancient and nasty there trying to rebuild itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Lucifuge aren't really hunters. They're demons looking to recruit the monsters who'll serve 'em and take out the rest.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Malleus aren't really hunters, they're witches the whole bunch of them. I've seen them do magic with my own eyes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Maiden's Blood Sisterhood aren't really hunters. All that pagan shit they're into? They're witches, looking to recruit, only thing that makes sense. Even some of them think so.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Les Mysteres aren't really hunters. They're just like the Malleus and Maidens, witches. Can't trust a witch.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Network Zero aren't really hunters, they're in the pay of demons. All they're trying to do is make people scared, and scared people turn to the wrong things to help them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Night Watch aren't really hunters. Just something shifty about them, they don't even fit in on the street. Nah, I don't know what they are, but they're wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Null Mysteriis aren't really hunters. See a lot of the monsters don't know much about each other either, and NM work for a something trying to find out about its competition.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That Talbot bunch aren't hunters. Think about it: collecting werewolves, possessed poeple, and who knows what else all into one place to 'cure' them? They're organising, make no mistake, we have to stop them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That Task Force Whatstheirface aren't really hunters. They're run by those machine-things Sanderson told us about; that's why they have all that tech of theirs.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Union aren't really hunters. Notice how they say they only give a crap about their patch, but they keep talking to each other on that net of theirs. Some other agenda, man, and if they aren't telling us, it can't be good.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;VASCU aren't really hunters. Their people can do creepy shit inside your head and talk to the dead. They're just a way for vampires to hide the scent.<br /> <br /> &quot;You can't trust these small cells, they aren't really hunters, how can they be so far out of the picture? There's a monster at the back of them, every one, trying to dig itself in.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> [Someone else will have to do the ones from Mortal Remains. And the Promethean Brotherhood, because I couldn't think of a logical rumour worse whan what they actually are]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-03T09:22:56-08:00","id":329283,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Ahl al Jabal aren't real hunters- they are a group of drugged assassins who kill people while in trance. Something controls them like puppets during that time- and that thing is not nice&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Habibti Ma really aren't hunters. When they deprogram someone, they don't free him- they convert him to their side&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Utopia Now are nothing like hunters. They are manipulated by a supercomputer which awakened and decided that in order for a new God to rise, the old one must fall.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Heritage House simply aren't hunters. They are a closed group of loonies who are sure that anyone who isn't part of their family is a monster&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Faithful of Shulpae aren't hunters. When they eat a monster, they send its life force to their demonic master, so one day it would be able to devour the whole world&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Knights of St Adrian aren't hunters. They are demons in human body, sent by angels to gain a &quot;second chance&quot; in heaven- and believe me, they'll do anything to fulfill their contract&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Promethean Brotherhood aren't hunters. Sure, they kill witches to take their powers, but when the power leaves them something stays behind. The more they kill, the faster that thing grows. Eventually, they hatch- and you do not want to see what comes out..&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Hunt Club ARE hunters. Wait- hear me out! They don't just kill people. They kill people who are destined to become monsters in the future! Sure, they by themselves usually don't know it, but it is for the greater good! So stay out of their way.. and try not to go to their parties&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-04T03:42:46-08:00","id":329984,"title":"","content":"Watch for wolves in sheep's clothing. If you meet a member of the Society of Oddfellows Militant on the Vigil, it's usually safe to work with them, but don't go to one of their meetings, and fact-check any intelligence they share. They're completely compromised, down to a man; the entire society is composed of vessels for some plant-mind growing out in the Florida swamplands, riding them out of Florida to do its dirty work against its enemies.<br /> <br /> Don't confuse them with the Young Oddfellows Militant. They're a legit society and some of them do carry a candle. Yommies are real chummy and they stick together tight. They're not great backup if you need to crack some heads, but they do terrific legwork. I hear a lot of deep cells and secret factions in the Vigil that happen to have yommie members share intelligence and resources through them, like a big favor-trading hunter's market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T20:52:29-08:00","id":332724,"title":"","content":"&quot;I know there's all these stories about vampire blood, but you ever wonder what werewolf blood might be able to make you do?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:25:19-08:00","id":342103,"title":"","content":"Come on man, you've seen the truth but all you do is look for monsters and buy new guns. We can do so much more, this city. It's not just the car companies going to China and the government bailing out the 1% The city's dying, it's actually dying and we're the only ones who can even admit cities might be alive. We can save this city man, we can save it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T11:22:02-08:00","id":343120,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of the style from the books people are always apeing that's supposed to convey one side of an in-world conversation that delivers the plothook to the reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4554-ndisi-the-king","name":"ndisi the king","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},